From c0b9ffe744d13e7709efb4ea298ae32f45a63158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:54:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] version capsule compatibility with uncached owner
 and child integrity gates

Keep legacy same-revision submission and require an explicit v2 contract across revisions. Withdraw availability on missing or dirty boot provenance, code skew, unsupported routes and unfiltered ledger unknowns. Bootstrap capsule children from the owner core and enforce its private expectation before execution and every late startup boundary. Preserve single-use authenticated rendezvous and startup cleanup.

Proof: witnessed behavioral RED/GREEN for submitter compatibility, boot/ledger/skew gates, child contract and late startup refusal; readiness addition RED then GREEN. Final focused six-file suite 74 passed; eight readiness consumers 35 passed; scripts/check 21 passed. Mutation harness baseline 51 passed, six distinct final-inventory/worker-route/late-boundary mutants killed; earlier six identity mutants also killed. Composed real submitter wire to owner placement/native main/execute/adoption/observation ends at intentional checkpoint failure, with explicit fixture seams; not private app/model or full historical-core proof. App ownership port and owner-controlled deployment remain separate incident gates.
